'''WHO LET RONALDO BATOT FLEE?''' — Akamatsu Group's money-laundering intermediary escaped Okaiken on 12 July, three days after arrests. Investigators found empty apartment 15 July. Worldwide arrest warrant issued 16 July. Four days too late.

'''AKAMATSU HEARING TOMORROW: WORKERS WAIT''' — July 17 court date. ¥18B pension fund audit enters third day. 12,000 employees still waiting for answers. Nishikawa evidence gives hope. IAA Commission: "Every yen accounted for."

'''BALISCAN WASTE: DAY 19, NO END IN SIGHT''' — Castejón blockade holds. 40,000 tonnes unmoved. Tanaka named three officials who told him inspections were "completed." All three reassigned. None charged.

