'''IAA COMMISSION: "ACCOUNTABILITY YOU CAN TRUST"''' — Chair Aoyama Reiko announced 12-investigator team dedicated to Akamatsu Group case. Nishikawa Daigo's evidence — 14 months of memos, email chains, 22-minute audio recording of Akamatsu Seijiro saying "the pension fund is not their money" — catalogued and verified. Aoyama commended the whistleblower: "This person had courage when the system did not." Commission also examining Batot's role as link between Akamatsu shell companies and Marítima Estrella shipping network.

'''NOTO BY-ELECTION: ACCOUNTABILITY ON THE BALLOT''' — July 26. Koda (LDP) vs Misaki (Coalition). Debate July 18 at Suzu Community Hall. Koda campaigns on "stability and recovery." Misaki campaigns on "accountability and change." IAA Commission jurisdiction over Noto red tide aftermath remains contested — Misaki: "The IAA should investigate who allowed the red tide response to fail. Noto deserves answers." LDP polling within margin of error. 10 days remain.

'''EMPEROR'S TROPHY: BRACKET MONDAY''' — 47 prefectural champions confirmed. Draw July 20 at Okami Imperial Palace. Crown Prince Tomohito presiding. Defending champion Noto Prefecture volleyball federation received wildcard after red tide disruption. Okami Metropolis and Toyozawa Metropolis seeded 1-2. Quarter-finals August 8, semi-finals August 9, final August 10 at Okami Metropolitan Gymnasium. Ehime Prefecture (seeded 4) returns after 12-year absence.

'''FM OVERSIGHT HEARING: JULY 22''' — PPO Diet committee scheduled open hearing. FM Nishimura to testify on 11-day silence, Castellano response, Ayorin community attacks. Coalition members pushed for open session — won. LDP members requested closed session for classified diplomatic content — denied. Deputy Director Hayashi Yuki to appear as witness. Ayorin community chair Burawa Yuki: "Eleven days of silence. One hearing. That is not accountability. That is a start."

'''NOPW EPISODE 4: KUROSHIO BOND FRACTURES''' — July 15, Naruto Arena (4,800). Kengo def. Akira Sato (14:22). Marcus Vance retained IC title (11:45, Vanguard Lock) — first defence since Mainichi interview. KAZUKI and Leoni forced to team against Big Stan and Diallo — won by DQ after Jusuf interference. Tension visible post-match. Island Invasion Tour August 9 sold out in 6 hours. Second show added August 10.

'''SESC REFORM: WHO WATCHES THE WATCHERS?''' — LDP Diet members proposed SESC Reform Bill: rotating audit firms every 5 years, mandatory whistleblower channels, criminal penalties for auditors who accept inducements. The bill follows the Kojima scandal — SESC auditor placed on leave after Ibuki supplemental indictment revealed auditor corruption. Coalition supports. PPO supports. But the question the Okami Times asks: who audits the SESC? The IAA Commission can investigate. But the Commission itself is appointed, not elected. accountability chains that end in appointment are not accountability chains. They are authority chains.

'''NATIONAL DIET: AUTUMN SESSION PREVIEW''' — Diet resumes July 21. Autumn budget begins August 4. Key bills: SESC Reform, DSA operational unit definition, IAA Commission budget supplemental. PM Ikazaki: "The autumn session will define this government's legacy." The Okami Times notes: the legacy will be defined by what the government does about the people who were failed — the 12,000 Akamatsu workers, the 14 Ayorin families, the Noto fishers. Not by what the government says about itself.

'''CYBERCRIME: TMPD EXPANDS DIGITAL UNIT''' — TMPD cybercrime division expanded from 40 to 65 officers. Commissioner Aoki: "Financial crime is digital crime." The expansion follows Akamatsu Group digital money laundering and MV Castellano case. The Okami Times notes: 65 officers for a metropolis of 8.2 million. The expansion is necessary. It is also insufficient.

